><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YAMORI, TAKAO</last-name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>HASE NAOKI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>TAKEUCHI SUSUMU</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>TAKEYASU TAKUMI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>TSUCHIYA NAOKI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>TSURUO TAKASHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>YAMORI TAKAO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>HASE, NAOKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>TAKEUCHI, SUSUMU</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>TAKEYASU, TAKUMI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>TSUCHIYA, NAOKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>TSURUO, TAKASHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YAMORI, TAKAO</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Anthranilic acid derivatives represented by general formulae (1) or (2) (wherein Y&lt;1&gt; and Y&lt;2&gt; are each a group represented by general formula (3)-1, (3)-2 or the like; X&lt;1&gt; is O, S or the like; X&lt;2&gt; is O or S; and R&lt;1&gt; to R&lt;4&gt; are each H or the like). These compounds have a cytotoxic activity and are therefore useful as cancer remedies, and they also exhibit an inhibitory activity against the production of IgE antibody and are useful as preventive or therapeutic agents for allergic diseases.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne des dérivés d'acide anthranilique qui correspondent aux formules générales (1) ou (2) où Y&lt;1&gt; et Y&lt;2&gt; représentent chacun un groupe correspondant à la formule générale (3)-1, (3)-2 ou analogue, X&lt;1&gt; représente O, S ou analogue, X&lt;2&gt; représente O ou S, tandis que les éléments R&lt;1&gt; à R&lt;4&gt; représentent chacun H ou analogue. Ces composés possèdent une action cytotoxique et peuvent ainsi être utilisés comme remèdes contre le cancer. Ils possèdent en outre une action inhibitrice à l'encontre de la production de l'anticorps IgE, et peuvent ainsi être utilisés comme agents préventifs ou thérapeutiques contre des maladies allergiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>